---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import BuyButton from '../components/BuyButton.astro';
import { site } from '../config';
---

<Base
  title="Refunds — stick"
  description="Cancel a pre-order any time before it ships. 30 days from delivery after that."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pt-16 pb-16 md:pt-24">
    <h1 class="headline text-hero">Refunds</h1>
    <p class="mt-9 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
      stick is a thing you buy to help you do something difficult. If it doesn’t
      help, we don’t want to keep your money and argue about it.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-14 space-y-12">
      <article class="rule pt-7">
        <h2 class="text-[22px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]">
          Before it ships: cancel any time
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          You’re buying a pre-order, and the first batch ships {site.shipWindow}.
          Until your order actually leaves, email us and we’ll refund the whole
          thing — price and shipping — no questions and no restocking fee.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="rule pt-7">
        <h2 class="text-[22px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]">
          After it arrives: 30 days
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          You have 30 days from delivery. Send the key back and we’ll refund what
          you paid for it. It can be used, opened, plugged in and covered in
          fingerprints — this is a thing you have to actually live with for a
          week or two to know, and a policy that only covers unopened boxes would
          be worthless.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Return postage is yours; the original shipping isn’t refunded after
          delivery. If the key arrives damaged or faulty, that’s on us — we cover
          postage both ways and you don’t need to be inside 30 days.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="rule pt-7">
        <h2 class="text-[22px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]">
          If it slips, you don’t have to chase us
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          If the ship date moves, we’ll email you and say so. You can take the
          refund at that point or wait — your choice, and asking for it costs you
          nothing.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="rule pt-7">
        <h2 class="text-[22px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]">
          Read the limits first, not after
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          The most common reason to want a refund on a product like this is
          discovering it can be defeated. We’ve written down exactly how, in
          detail, before you buy —
          <a href="/limits" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4"
            >what stick can’t do</a
          >. If that page changes your mind, we’d much rather it changed it now.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="rule pt-7">
        <h2 class="text-[22px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]">
          How to start one
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          {
            site.supportEmail ? (
              <>
                Email{' '}
                <a
                  href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}
                  class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4"
                >
                  {site.supportEmail}
                </a>{' '}
                with your order number. We answer {site.unlockResponseTime}.
              </>
            ) : (
              <span class="text-key">
                TODO — no support address exists yet. A refund policy nobody can
                invoke is not a refund policy; this must be filled in before the
                buy button goes live.
              </span>
            )
          }
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="rule bg-mist">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-20">
      <h2 class="headline text-display">Still want one?</h2>
      <p class="mt-6 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
        {site.price} + shipping, one time. Ships {site.shipWindow}.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-9">
        <BuyButton size="lg" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
